# Check every text file out with LF, whatever the machine's core.autocrlf says. Git for Windows
# defaults to autocrlf=true, and the compose stack bind-mounts scripts/ and deploy/ into Linux
# containers: a CRLF `#!/usr/bin/env bash` there fails as "can't execute 'bash\r'", which took the
# backup sidecar down on the first Windows install from a git checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf
# cmd.exe needs CRLF in a batch file. It is committed with CRLF, so leave its bytes alone.
*.bat -text
